%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: b8c5f8bea1b438d4687ad9b712e77c3e, type: 3}
  m_Name: Level 1-14 Starting Cutscene
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::CutsceneData
  line:
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: I hurried to Hong Kong as soon as I could, and sent my parents a letter
      asking permission to join them. My brother-in-law Manuel Hidalgo was deported
      under the governor of La Laguna, stating that Filipinos were mistaken in thinking
      that the new Civic Code gave them any rights.
    isLeftSide: 0
    pose: 1
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: When I arrived there, I learned that my brother Paciano had been released
      from exile in Mindoro, but that three of my sisters had been summoned with
      the probability of deportation.
    isLeftSide: 0
    pose: 3
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: A trap was set for us to get me into the government's hands. They targeted
      my mother and sister. I was angry at this fact, but I remained where I am as
      my parents told me to not come to Manila.
    isLeftSide: 0
    pose: 5
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: I was already acquainted with most of the Filipino colony, including
      Jose M. Basa, who was a fearsome fellow who managed to get out of proclamations.
      He helped me with a few things, one of which was a case against me. I am grateful
      for that.
    isLeftSide: 0
    pose: 4
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: Eventually then, a free portion of my family came to Hong Kong. I was
      licensed to practice medicine in the colony, operating as an oculist with notable
      success.
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 4
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: I went on a voyage to British North Borneo and with Mr. Pryor, to look
      over vacant lands which were offered to me by the Company, for a Filipino colony.
      I hope that the people from Calamba can at least thrive here, without being
      in constant threat or living in fear when the Spaniards come their way.
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 2
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: Another Governor-General succeeded General Wyler, who I know is General
      Despujol. I applauded his efforts in regards to seeking reform. I eventually
      had the opportunity to talk to him in his place. On the way there, I was with
      my sister Lucia. We had made our way to the residency of the Governor-General.
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 0
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: 'We then talked about different things, and eventually ended up asking
      if I were to still go with my original plan of letting the Filipino colony
      settle at North Borneo. I stood firm with my decision that they will stay there,
      as the land troubles at Calamba left them with uncertainty in the trust of
      the government in the Philippines. '
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 2
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: I wanted them to at least live free without worry of being victims
      of abuse in power. The bitterness in both parties could not be easily forgotten.
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 0
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: I wanted them to at least live free without worry of being victims
      of abuse in power. The bitterness in both parties could not be easily forgotten.
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 0
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: "With the General respecting my decision, he then brought up the five
      \"Poor Friars\" handbills. He said he found them in the roll of my bedding
      sent with Rizal\u2019s baggage to the custom house, and asked whose they could
      be."
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 1
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: Rizal answered that of course the General knew that the bedding belonged
      to his sister Lucia, but she was no fool and would not have secreted in a place
      where they were certain to be found five little papers which, hidden within
      her camisa or placed in her stocking, would have been absolutely sure to come
      in unnoticed.
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 2
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: Because of that, I was ordered to be taken prisoner to Fort Santiago.
      I do not know why I had been framed for a crime I did not commit, but I could
      do nothing about it. As they were firm in their decision. Instead of me going
      home with my family in Hong Kong, I am deported to Dapitan.
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 6
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: Because of that, I was ordered to be taken prisoner to Fort Santiago.
      I do not know why I had been framed for a crime I did not commit, but I could
      do nothing about it. As they were firm in their decision. Instead of me going
      home with my family in Hong Kong, I am deported to Dapitan.
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 6
  - speakerName: Narrator
    speakerType: 2
    hero: {fileID: 0}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: Chapter VI The Period of Propaganda. End.
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 6
  - speakerName: Narrator
    speakerType: 2
    hero: {fileID: 0}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: Chapter VII The Execution of Rizal. Start.
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 6
